---
description: Prefer shipping preventable hardening now over deferring until incidents
alwaysApply: true
---

# Do preventive work now

When a gap is identified (bot protection, validation, missing tests for a risky path, ops checklist, etc.) and it can be done in the current task without blocking higher-priority work, **implement it now** rather than parking it as “add later if problems arise.”

## Apply especially to

- Public abuse surfaces (forms, signup, contact, reactivation)
- Security checks that already have a pattern elsewhere in the repo (extend the pattern)
- Small hardening that reuses existing env keys / helpers

## Still defer when

- The user explicitly asks to defer
- The work needs external dashboard/config the agent cannot complete and a manual note is enough for that turn
- Scope would balloon past the user’s request (then do the minimal preventive slice and say what remains)
